=>Install Shopify CLI (One Time)
npm install -g @shopify/cli @shopify/theme

=>Login to Shopify
shopify auth login

Verify:shopify auth whoami

=>Create Your Project Folder
mkdir bourgee-theme
cd bourgee-theme

=>Pull the Theme From Store
If you know the Theme ID:
shopify theme pull \
--store bourgee-international-demo.myshopify.com \
--theme <THEME_ID>

=>Or first list available themes:
shopify theme list \
--store bourgee-international-demo.myshopify.com

=>Start Local Development
shopify theme dev \
--store bourgee-international-demo.myshopify.com

=>Shopify CLI will provide URLs similar to:
Local:
http://127.0.0.1:9292

Preview:
https://xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx.ngrok.io

=>Changes are synced automatically.

=>No manual refresh is usually required because Shopify CLI hot reloads changes.

=>Check Theme Before Upload
shopify theme check

This helps identify Liquid, JSON, and Shopify best-practice issues.

=>Push Changes
Upload the current theme:
shopify theme push \
--store bourgee-international-demo.myshopify.com

=>Or push to a specific theme:

shopify theme push \
--store bourgee-international-demo.myshopify.com \
--theme <THEME_ID>

=>Pull Latest Changes (If Someone Else Modified the Theme)
shopify theme pull \
--store bourgee-international-demo.myshopify.com




# Login
shopify auth login

# Check current account
shopify auth whoami

# List themes
shopify theme list --store bourgee-international-demo.myshopify.com

# Pull theme
shopify theme pull --store bourgee-international-demo.myshopify.com

# Start development
shopify theme dev --store bourgee-international-demo.myshopify.com

# Upload changes
shopify theme push --store bourgee-international-demo.myshopify.com

# Download latest changes
shopify theme pull --store bourgee-international-demo.myshopify.com

# Delete local cache if needed
shopify cache clear

# Validate theme
shopify theme check